---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description={`About ${SITE.name} — neutral crypto news, signals, and a data API, operated by ${SITE.operator}.`}
  path="/about"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Signals, not noise.</h1>

      <p>
        {SITE.name} is a crypto market-data publication and a documented data API. We publish original daily
        market briefs written from numbers we collect ourselves, attributed news digests that always name and
        link their source, and one plain daily direction signal per tracked coin. It is operated by{' '}
        {SITE.operator}.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Market briefs:</strong> original prose written only from our own collected price and market data — one per day.</li>
        <li><strong>News digests:</strong> a short summary of a story published elsewhere, in our own words, always naming and linking the source. We never rewrite or reproduce other publishers' articles.</li>
        <li><strong>Signals:</strong> deterministic indicators (momentum, trend, volatility) → one direction word per tracked coin per day — <code>Rising</code>, <code>Falling</code>, <code>Steady</code>, or <code>Choppy</code> — with the measured reason. Never "buy", never "sell", never a fake confidence score.</li>
        <li><strong>API:</strong> one <code>X-API-Key</code> unlocks signals, prices, market, and news.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How it runs</h2>
      <p>
        The platform operates itself on schedules and automation, with a human editor accountable for what is
        published. It runs on our own low-cost infrastructure and aims to stay lean, portable, and cheap to
        operate. See our <a href="/editorial-policy">editorial policy</a> for how content is produced.
      </p>

      <h2>Principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Neutral, not hyped.</strong> Banned hype words, no CTAs, no price targets.</li>
        <li><strong>Attributed.</strong> Sources are always linked; API use requires attribution.</li>
        <li><strong>Machine-readable.</strong> Stable response shapes and documented limits.</li>
        <li><strong>Not advice.</strong> Informational only, always.</li>
      </ul>

      <p><a href="/get-access" class="btn btn-primary">Get a free API key</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
